{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759641-a-world-of-future-darkness","id":759641,"title":"A world of Future Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-06T19:19:45-08:00","id":759641,"title":"A world of Future Darkness","content":"I was digging through some old White Wolf magazines and came across the article 'A world of Future Darkness' by Deirdre Brooks. It had a write up for using mainly VtA in a Cyber Punk 2020 setting. It has rules for how the Camarilla and others had adapted to the world as cybernetics and Megacorps spread. Included rules for using the cybernetics and their effect on vampire bodies. There is a new discipline called Technica, which allows a vampire to control and interact with machines and computers. I was wondering if anyone had ever used anything out of this in their games or if anyone had even really looked at it? I'd like to hear what people thought about it? Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T19:50:41-08:00","id":759656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759641-a-world-of-future-darkness#post759641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was digging through some old White Wolf magazines and came across the article 'A world of Future Darkness' by Deirdre Brooks. It had a write up for using mainly VtA in a Cyber Punk 2020 setting. It has rules for how the Camarilla and others had adapted to the world as cybernetics and Megacorps spread. Included rules for using the cybernetics and their effect on vampire bodies. There is a new discipline called Technica, which allows a vampire to control and interact with machines and computers. I was wondering if anyone had ever used anything out of this in their games or if anyone had even really looked at it? I'd like to hear what people thought about it? Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>My friends and I went the easy route back in the 90's and just did a Shadowrun 'port (it, naturally, handles supernaturals better than Cyberpunk from the outset by dint of already having supernatural splats). I played a vampire in a WoD/Shadowrun hybrid, no muss, no fuss. We all liked it. (Even without cross-porting, it's very easy as-presented to advance Masquerade 50 or 100+ years into the future by just adapting a few Mage or similar rules/concepts and making up a couple new disciplines. Easy-peasy.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T07:07:49-08:00","id":759968,"title":"","content":"Wow, talk about your basic blast from the past. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There were three articles actually - part two was &quot;Night City by Night&quot; and part three was an adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-07-2015, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T14:18:07-08:00","id":760208,"title":"","content":"Any idea what Demons or the imbued look like at that point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:38:48-08:00","id":760278,"title":"","content":"Downloaded from DriveThruRPG and reading now :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T17:57:21-08:00","id":760375,"title":"","content":"Just John, how easy was it to use Shadowrun? I don't own a rule set at this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T18:05:39-08:00","id":760378,"title":"","content":"I'm not Just John but I've also adapted WoD stuff to Shadowrun during second and third edition. It worked fairly well, although the powers required some tuning to work right. Things work surprisingly well as long as everything is respected. Like, hedge magic can't access the Matrix, but awakened sphere magick can because Virtual Adepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T20:28:10-08:00","id":760453,"title":"","content":"The rules look pretty good. I'd say Mage cybernetics and their systems should trump those in Cyberpunk, though. They wouldn't carry Paradox in non-mages, but I might use the Paradox ratings instead as the amount of Humanity you lose. Quintessence could be replaced by Blood, as would any other fuel or expenditure required to get the cybernetic to work. Excessive enhancements might also mean the vampire has to spend extra vitae to rise each night, fuelling the cybernetics through the Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 11-08-2015, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T20:39:51-08:00","id":760459,"title":"","content":"There's no reason that cybernetics that are relatively common among sleepers should cause paradox for mages. That's like completely contrary to how Mage works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T22:24:54-08:00","id":760508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759641-a-world-of-future-darkness?p=760459#post760459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason that cybernetics that are relatively common among sleepers should cause paradox for mages. That's like completely contrary to how Mage works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Book of the Weaver had them as normal, everyday Devices that didn't require anything special. However, for shapeshifters, they had to be fetishes, and any bonuses were halved relative to the rating (Device 4 that would give +4 to Strength changed to Fetish 4 that would only give +2 to Strength, for example)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T01:25:58-08:00","id":760565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759641-a-world-of-future-darkness?p=760459#post760459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason that cybernetics that are relatively common among sleepers should cause paradox for mages. That's like completely contrary to how Mage works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep forgetting that it's 2020, and you're quite right. I still think the permadox ratings make a good indication of Humanity lost, however. The Cyberpunk 2020 conversion has a system more in line with Cyberpunk's, but it involves quite a bit more maths. <br /> <br /> What do people think of the new Discipline that's offered, and the Thaumaturgical ritual to allow vampires to have cybernetics? My initial thought was that the only way to make cybernetics permanent was for the surgery itself to inflict aggravated damage, as this kind of damage often leaves scars in vampires, so would theoretically allow permanent implants as well. The damage would be comparable to the size of the implant (one for an eye, two for a forearm, three for a leg, etc).<br /> <br /> Some of the cybernetics listed are also really, really overpowered, which is another reason to defer to the cybernetics in Mage (one example has a starting vampire PC with the equivalent of nine dots of Celerity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T01:27:41-08:00","id":760567,"title":"","content":"Needing them to be fetishes makes sense simply because Garou need to be able to shapeshift.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to die on a hill here, though. Just didn't agree with that particular suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T01:37:57-08:00","id":760570,"title":"","content":"Garou with cybernetics would be tainted by the Weaver otherwise, too. I imagine Gaia would be happy with prosthetic limbs and pacemakers, perhaps even minor cosmetics, but anything too technological would otherwise interfere too much with their bodies and possibly prevent them from becoming werewolves in the first place. Making the cybernetics fetishes would sidestep (haha) that problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T07:21:41-08:00","id":760655,"title":"","content":"You don't &quot;become&quot; a shapeshifter. You are born one from the get go. If something is inside your body when you shapeshift you will rip it the hell out and scar yourself, but it's not a problem as the shifters have amazing health benefits. That's why shifter cybernetics are fetishes so that they integrate with the shifter's body and can shift with them.<br /> <br /> The whole practice is weaverish by itself, but Gaia doesn't care either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:35:15-08:00","id":760792,"title":"","content":"You can tell I don't play Werewolf :-P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T17:08:07-08:00","id":761848,"title":"","content":"For those of you that have used Shadowrun, with CWoD, was it a Shadowrun game with CWoD incorporated or CWoD with Shadowrun incorporated? If you ported over the cybertech from Shadowrun, how did you do it? Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T17:20:30-08:00","id":761853,"title":"","content":"It was Shadowrun with CWoD ported into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}